            "anchor": "logic-and-shift-instructions-shl",
            "startLine": 14702,
            "endLine": 14703
          },
          "quotation": "Shift bits left, zero-fill on right."
        },
        {
          "evidenceId": "PTX-9.3-SHL-003",
          "sourceKind": "HTML",
          "documentPath": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
          "documentSha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
          "locator": {
            "section": "9.7.8.8",
            "heading": "Logic and Shift Instructions: shl",
            "anchor": "logic-and-shift-instructions-shl",
            "startLine": 14705,
            "endLine": 14707
          },
          "quotation": "shl.type d, a, b;\n\n.type = { .b16, .b32, .b64 };"
        },
        {
          "evidenceId": "PTX-9.3-SHL-004",
          "sourceKind": "HTML",
          "documentPath": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
          "documentSha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
          "locator": {
            "section": "9.7.8.8",
            "heading": "Logic and Shift Instructions: shl",
            "anchor": "logic-and-shift-instructions-shl",
            "startLine": 14710,
            "endLine": 14711
          },
          "quotation": "Shift a left by the amount specified by unsigned 32-bit value in b."
        },
        {
          "evidenceId": "PTX-9.3-SHL-005",
          "sourceKind": "HTML",
          "documentPath": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
          "documentSha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
          "locator": {
            "section": "9.7.8.8",
            "heading": "Logic and Shift Instructions: shl",
            "anchor": "logic-and-shift-instructions-shl",
            "startLine": 14712,
            "endLine": 14715
          },
          "quotation": "d = a << b;"
        },
        {
          "evidenceId": "PTX-9.3-SHL-006",
          "sourceKind": "HTML",
          "documentPath": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
          "documentSha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
          "locator": {
            "section": "9.7.8.8",
            "heading": "Logic and Shift Instructions: shl",
            "anchor": "logic-and-shift-instructions-shl",
            "startLine": 14718,
            "endLine": 14719
          },
          "quotation": "Shift amounts greater than the register width N are clamped to N."
        },
        {
          "evidenceId": "PTX-9.3-SHL-007",
          "sourceKind": "HTML",
          "documentPath": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
          "documentSha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
          "locator": {
            "section": "9.7.8.8",
            "heading": "Logic and Shift Instructions: shl",
            "anchor": "logic-and-shift-instructions-shl",
            "startLine": 14719,
            "endLine": 14720
          },
          "quotation": "The sizes of the destination and first source operand must match, but not necessarily the type. The b operand must be a 32-bit value, regardless of the instruction type."
        },
        {
          "evidenceId": "PTX-9.3-SHL-010",
          "sourceKind": "HTML",
          "documentPath": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
          "documentSha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
          "locator": {
            "section": "9.2",
            "heading": "PTX Instructions",
            "anchor": "ptx-instructions",
            "startLine": 7513,
            "endLine": 7525
          },
          "quotation": "PTX instructions generally have from zero to four operands, plus an optional guard predicate appearing after an @ symbol to the left of the opcode:\n@p opcode;\n@p opcode a;\n@p opcode d, a;\n@p opcode d, a, b;\n@p opcode d, a, b, c;\nFor instructions that create a result value, the d operand is the destination operand, while a, b, and c are source operands."
        },
        {
          "evidenceId": "PTX-9.3-SHL-011",
          "sourceKind": "HTML",
          "documentPath": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
          "documentSha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
          "locator": {
            "section": "9.7.13.2",
            "heading": "Control Flow Instructions: @",
            "anchor": "control-flow-instructions-at",
            "startLine": 21826,
            "endLine": 21840
          },
          "quotation": "9.7.13.2. Control Flow Instructions: @\n@\nPredicated execution.\n@{!}p    instruction;\nExecute an instruction or instruction block for threads that have the guard predicate True. Threads with a False guard predicate do nothing."
        },
        {
          "evidenceId": "PTX-9.3-SHL-012",
          "sourceKind": "HTML",
          "documentPath": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
          "documentSha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
          "locator": {
            "section": "9.3",
            "heading": "Predicated Execution",
            "anchor": "predicated-execution",
            "startLine": 7537,
            "endLine": 7549
          },
          "quotation": "All instructions have an optional guard predicate which controls conditional execution of the instruction. The syntax to specify conditional execution is to prefix an instruction with @{!}p, where p is a predicate variable, optionally negated. Instructions without a guard predicate are executed unconditionally."
        },
        {
          "evidenceId": "PTX-9.3-SHL-013",
          "sourceKind": "HTML",
          "documentPath": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
          "documentSha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
          "locator": {
            "section": "9.7.13.2",
            "heading": "Control Flow Instructions: @",
            "anchor": "control-flow-instructions-at",
            "startLine": 21840,
            "endLine": 21842
          },
          "quotation": "If {!}p then instruction\nIntroduced in PTX ISA version 1.0.\nSupported on all target architectures."
        }
